# UI & product tone

## Brand

- Logo: `logo-mark` / Fugaz One; teal `#0f766e` (light) / brighter on dark
- Body: Plus Jakarta Sans (self-hosted `public/fonts/` + `src/lib/fonts.css`); CSS vars in `src/index.css` (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--logo`, `--partner-a/b/common/other`). Do not reintroduce Google Fonts `@import` (causes logo FOUT).
- Theme: class `.dark` on `html` + `@custom-variant dark` in `index.css` (not `prefers-color-scheme`). Muted copy: `text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400`. Charts: `axisTick` / `legendLabel` / `tipProps` from `chart-theme.ts`; dark tooltips also forced via `.recharts-default-tooltip` in `index.css`.
- Partner identity: blue A / rose B / violet common / amber other (not brand teal) — `src/lib/partners.ts` + `OwnerBadge`
- Boot/setup/lock share `AuthShell` + `.logo-mark-on-light` (no flat `--bg` splash — avoids flash)

Tone: private couple’s OS — not bank SaaS. Sync = “vault / GitHub”, not “our cloud.”
Never show formula letters (X / Y / Z) in UI copy — use plain words (income, expenses, **Net**, left after expenses / short this month via `netCaption`). Partner fair slice of Net is **Net share** (not “Keeps”) — fairness target on combined leftover, not each person’s bank balance.

## Dates & money

- UI dates: **DD/MM/YYYY** via `src/lib/dates.ts`
- Month labels: **MM/YYYY** compact; Home cards + Track hub list titles **MMMM YYYY** (`formatMonthName`) so they don’t look like money
- Money: always euro — `formatMoney` / `MoneyInput` / `parseLocaleNumber` (no currency Settings)

## Structure

- Primitives: `src/components/ui/*`
- Nav: Home, Track, History, Incomes, Expenses, Outlook (text); Settings as header icon with sync/theme/lock
- Logo **Tandem** → Home (`/`); Home also first nav tab. Track at `/track`
- Page titles: shared sticky `PageHeader`; pages wrap in `PageShell` (body `z-0`, no `isolate`). Sticky title/Settings: no `transform` / fade / box-shadow (GPU layers blur text on mobile scroll); absolute fill seal + app-header strip; subtitle `14px/20px`. `overflow-x: clip` on `html` only. Sticky chrome + mobile nav + Track editor footer stay **opaque**.
- Type hierarchy: **Page** `PageHeader` → **Section** `SectionHeading` / `CardTitle` (sentence case, display weight) → **Meta** `MetaLabel` / table th / form Label (tiny uppercase only). Never use MetaLabel styling for major section titles (Outlook Looking ahead, Track hub, MonthEditor Incomes/Expenses/Notes, etc.)
- Track (`/track`) = hub + inline month editor (`MonthEditor`); tracked-months list read-only until section pencil (Banks-style; check to exit); then per-row open + delete. Rows: month · left-aligned In/Out/**Net** (label over amount; negative Net uses Outlook orange). Narrow: metrics on a second row under month (+ actions while editing); `sm+`: one row with fixed-width money columns. Editor sticky footer = three equal metric parts (Household · partner A · partner B); Household net shortLabel **Net**, long label sign-aware (`netCaption`); split toggle on the Cancel/Save row. Keep editor bottom padding ≥ footer height so Expenses **Add to month** is not covered; Save flushes pending card-sheet amounts.
- Home = horizontal snap scroller (all tracked months + next estimate); thumb-drag follows the strip then smooth-settles; status meta (Estimate / Not tracked) on the same line as the month title so card content doesn’t shift down (no “Tracked” / “Current”); month title slightly smaller + muted (`text-stone-600` / calendar teal) so **Net** stays the stronger figure; caption `netCaption` (left after expenses / short this month); Net + partner **Net share** use Outlook orange when negative; partner **Income** + **Pays** + **Net share** on cards; settle line when card payment data exists; no Track/History/Outlook CTAs on Home (empty vault still offers track / samples)
- Track hub list: full month name (`October 2026`) in display type; calendar month in teal (no “current” label)
- Track footer: Pays = fair share of expenses (not card charge); Net share = fair slice of household Net (not account balance); settlement line when `paymentByOwner` has data (expenses only — does not equalise Net share)
- Settings uses sticky sub-tabs: Household / Categories / Banks / Vault / Security (auto-lock + password) / Data; keep short plain-English helper notes on confusing controls (Household split: **50/50** · **By income** · **Income · equal Net**; callout explains Pays vs Net share per mode)
- Track editor sections: **Incomes**, **Expenses** (card chips + shared bank labels + month totals), optional **Notes**
- History = income vs expense (tracked actuals only — no dashed forward projections), **Net** bars (cumulative caption), partner **Net share** lines, category trends, expense mix (varied series hues, not all teal); Outlook = hero Σ **Net** + month net bars; looking-ahead Income / Expenses €/% / **Net** €/%; Net tile in teal; no separate Savings tile; don’t repeat avg as “next €same” hints; no expenses-vs-net strip bar; no multi-month projection table (baseline tiles are enough)
- Chart legends: click toggles series visibility (`useLegendFilter`); dim/strike hidden labels; reset when range changes
- Pie charts: `PieBreakdown` (donut left, €/% rows fill remaining width; two columns when ≥5 slices); same card layout on History + Expenses mix; do not rely on Recharts Legend for pie filter (shared `dataKey: "value"`)
- Expenses table: category rows × month columns (not the reverse)
- Analytics tables (Expenses / Incomes / Outlook): first label column uses `.analytics-sticky-label` (`sticky left-0` + opaque `--bg`) so names stay visible while month/metric columns scroll horizontally
- History/Incomes/Expenses/Outlook range toggle sticks under the app header while scrolling (`PageHeader` + `overflow-x: clip`)
- Prefer existing Button/Card/Input/Select patterns and stone/teal Tailwind usage
- Dropdowns: always `Select` from `src/components/ui/select.tsx` (appearance-none + inset ChevronDown) — no raw browser `<select>`
- Clickable controls: `cursor-pointer` on hover (Button base + nav / raw `<button>`s)
- Motion: subtle on page bodies only — never animate opacity/transform on sticky title bands (mobile blur)

## Shortcuts (preserve)

- `Ctrl/Cmd+N` start tracking current month and open `/track` · `Ctrl/Cmd+S` save month or push
